    "number": 128,
    "summary": "Blessed are those who fear the Lord and walk in His ways.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Blessed is every one that feareth the Lord; that walketh in his ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy shalt thou be, and it shall be well with thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "2 Ne. 13:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Isa. 3:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Health."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 57
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 66
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy wife shall be as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Husbands."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Ps. 134:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Zion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s children, and peace upon Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Ps. 125:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
